-- lib/autodiff.cub — differentiation of polynomials as a program about programs (the example of F31 in
-- PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.13 “F31–F32 — Reflection and certificates”, its part F31). Loaded after lib/ring.cub. D is the symbolic derivative over the codes of
-- polynomials in one variable; fwd is forward-mode automatic differentiation (dual numbers);
-- fwd-der: the two agree; taylor: D is the derivative of the function the code denotes, in the
-- form that makes sense over Nat: p(x + h) = p(x) + h·p'(x) + h²·q for some q. Each inductive
-- step of taylor is a ring identity, proved by one evaluation of lib/ring.cub's normalizer.
data Pl = kc (n : Nat) | kx | kadd (a : Pl) (b : Pl) | kmul (a : Pl) (b : Pl)
